# Vehicle bays: always run and save

After changing `blender/table/vehicle_bays.py`, adding vehicle assets under `models/`, or when the user expects props to appear in a `.blend`, **do not** claim the scene is updated until Blender has been run **and** the file has been written back.

## Required command pattern

Use **`SAVE_BLEND_AFTER=1`** so `vehicle_bays.py` calls `bpy.ops.wm.save_mainfile` at the end (see script `if __name__` block). Without it, headless runs leave **no change on disk** when the user opens the file later.

From the repo root (adjust Blender binary if needed):

```bash
SAVE_BLEND_AFTER=1 /Applications/Blender.app/Contents/MacOS/Blender \
  --background blender/main.blend \
  --python blender/table/vehicle_bays.py
```

Repeat for any other working blend that contains the desk (e.g. `blender/test.blend`) so parallel workflows stay in sync.

`vehicle_bays.py` uses simple fixed layout constants at the top of the file (not `build_table.py`).

## Verification

Console must include **`Info: Saved "<name>.blend"`** (or equivalent save confirmation). Optionally grep `[vehicle_bays]` lines for OK / scene summary.

## Viewport reminder

Vehicles exist only in **Main Scene** (see `.cursor/rules/blender-table-front.mdc`). **circuit-elements** will still look empty.
